{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>I am YHWH who brought you out of Ur of the Chaldees, etc.</b> The Ramban, of blessed memory, explained: from the time I brought you out of Ur of the Chaldees and performed a miracle for you, it was My will to give you this land. But now He did not decree that He would give it to him; rather, He said that He had brought him out of Ur of the Chaldees with the intention of giving it to him. Therefore Abraham was troubled lest there be a condition of deeds attached to the inheritance of the land, even though He had said several times, 'To your seed I will give this land' — for now He did not decree the gift as He had decreed the seed to him. Therefore he said, 'By what shall I know that I shall inherit it?' And he did not ask for a sign, and the Holy One, blessed be He, did not deal with him as with the rest of the signs, to show him a sign or a wonder in a marvelous thing; rather, Abraham asked to know with true knowledge that he would inherit it, and that his sin or his seed's sin would not cause it to be withheld from them, or perhaps the Canaanites might repent. And the Holy One, blessed be He, cut with him this covenant that he would inherit it in any case:" "<b>And in the Midrash:</b> 'I am YHWH who brought you out of Ur of the Chaldees' — at the hour our father Abraham, peace be upon him, was born, one star arose in the east and swallowed four stars to the four directions of heaven. The wise men said to Nimrod: a son was born to Terah at this hour, who is destined to produce from himself a nation that will inherit this world and the world to come. If you wish, let his father be given a houseful of silver and gold, and let us kill him. Immediately Nimrod sent to his father; he said to him: a son was born to you yesterday; now give him to me and we will kill him, and I will give you a houseful of silver and gold. Terah said to him: I will tell you a parable — to what may the matter be compared? To a horse to whom they said: let us cut off your head and we will give you a houseful of barley. The horse said to them: fools! If you cut off my head, who will eat the barley? And you — if you kill my son, who will inherit the silver and the gold? The king replied: from your words I recognize that a son was indeed born to you. Terah said to him: a son was born to me — and he died. He said to him: as surely as I live, I say this about a living one and not a dead one. What did Terah do? He hid his son in a cave for three years. The Holy One, blessed be He, prepared for him two openings: from one oil went out, and from the other fine flour. When he was three years old he went out from the cave. He pondered in his heart: who created heaven and earth and me? He prayed all day long to the sun. In the evening the sun set in the west and the moon rose in the east. When he saw the moon and the stars around the moon, he said: this is what created heaven and earth and me, and these stars are its officers and servants. He stood all night in prayer to the moon. In the morning the moon set in the west and the sun rose in the east. He said: these have no power; there is a Master over them — to Him I will pray and to Him I will bow. He went to his father and said to him: my father, who created heaven and earth and me? His father said to him: my god created heaven and earth and all these. He said to him: Abraham, show me your god — perhaps they have power to create all these? Immediately he brought his idol and showed him his god. Abraham returned to his mother and said to her: my mother, prepare for me nice and good dishes and I will bring them to my father's god, perhaps they will accept my offering from me. Immediately his mother prepared him nice and good dishes and he brought them to his father's god and placed them before the largest of them — and there was no voice and no answer. He returned to his mother and said to her: prepare me nice and good dishes like the first ones. She prepared them for him and he brought them before his father's idol — and there was no voice and no answer. Immediately the Shekhinah rested upon him and he called out concerning them: 'A mouth to them and they do not speak; eyes to them and they do not see.' Immediately he took fire and burned them, and brought the largest of them outside and placed the hammer in its hand. When his father came to his house and found his gods burned, he said to Abraham: my son, why did you burn my gods? He said: I did not burn them; rather, the largest of them grew angry at them and burned them. He said to him: my son, you fool — do they have power or the spirit of life that they could do all this? Why, I myself made them from wood! He said to him: let your ears hear what your mouth speaks — and if they have no power, why did you tell me 'my god created heaven and earth'? What did Terah do? He went to Nimrod and said to him: my son burned my gods and your gods with fire. Nimrod sent for Abraham and said to him: why did you do this? He said: I did not do this, but the largest did. Nimrod said: do they have the spirit of life that they could do such a thing? He said to him: let your ears hear what you speak with your mouth — and if they have no power, why do you abandon the One who created heaven and earth and bow down to wood? He said to him: I created heaven and earth by my power. Abraham said to him: you are able to create? When I went out from the cave I saw the sun rising in the east and setting in the west — do you make it rise in the west and set in the east, and I will bow down to you. And if not, He who strengthened my hand to burn the idols — He will strengthen me and I will kill you. Nimrod said to his wise men: what shall be the judgment of this one? They said to him: this is the one of whom we said about him, a nation is destined to come forth from him that will inherit this world and the world to come. And now, according to the very law he did, so shall be done to him. Immediately they threw him into the fiery furnace. At that hour the Holy One, blessed be He, was filled with mercy for him and saved him, as it is said: 'I am YHWH who brought you out of Ur of the Chaldees.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:12:45.791788763Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}